{% schema %}
  {
    
    "name": "Section 4",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-550181345406485472 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/e49d78-3/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_STATIC&editorId=549541555719897919&sectionId=550181345406485472)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggqQ5fWFh4N_text","label":"ggqQ5fWFh4N_text","default":"<p><strong>THE DIFFERENT FORMS OF SHILAJIT</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gufyPityYGUvN_text","label":"gufyPityYGUvN_text","default":"<p><strong>Extract (Resin): </strong>is the purest form of shilajit. It is a sticky, black substance that is collected from the rocks in the Himalayan mountains. Shilajit resin has a long history in Ayurvedic medicine. Recognized for its performance-enhancing properties, it has been utilized by Russian Special Forces for over 40 years to improve strength, recovery, and muscle mass.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggayTO6TPwj_text","label":"ggayTO6TPwj_text","default":"<p><strong>Powder: </strong>Shilajit powder is made by grinding shilajit resin into a fine powder. It is typically mixed with water or juice and then consumed.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggOJ0HnHxqc_text","label":"ggOJ0HnHxqc_text","default":"<p><strong>Caplets:</strong> Shilajit caps provide a convenient and tasteless way to consume it. They can be more potent than the resin, assuming the brand is using a quality extract.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggYNaVI0EY3_text","label":"ggYNaVI0EY3_text","default":"<p><strong>Gummies:</strong> Ease of use and controlled dosage makes gummies ideal for daily consumption...but only if you can find one that tastes great.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gWQamTyJaiZIn_text","label":"gWQamTyJaiZIn_text","default":"<p><strong>Quality Matters in Gummies &amp; Supplements</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"grqEXPgCtpeHH_text","label":"grqEXPgCtpeHH_text","default":"<p><strong>Low Shilajit Potency</strong>: Contains&nbsp;10-20% fulvic acid</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-1_text","label":"gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-1_text","default":"<p><strong>Flavoring:</strong> Often flavored with added sugars and artificial flavors.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-2_text","label":"gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-2_text","default":"<p><strong>Absorption:</strong> Processing may reduce the absorption of beneficial compounds.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggirBNt77qf_text","label":"ggirBNt77qf_text","default":"<p><strong>Sourcing:</strong> Typically sourced from lower elevations, potentially impacting quality and potency.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggR6PjDBjvz_text","label":"ggR6PjDBjvz_text","default":"<p><strong>Grade and Effectiveness:</strong> May be lower grade and less effective due to processing and lower-quality sourcing.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gytBzFzxYdrhk_text","label":"gytBzFzxYdrhk_text","default":"<p><strong>HOT TIP</strong></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gSwQScGxVHdUb_text","label":"gSwQScGxVHdUb_text","default":"<p>When choosing shilajit, prioritize quality and safety. Look for brands with lab reports showing high Fulvic Acid and no heavy metals. Choose easy-to-use forms. High-quality shilajit is often dark, sticky, and has an earthy smell. Always rely on lab reports for the most accurate assessment.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gGsBdFFGBlWmW_text","label":"gGsBdFFGBlWmW_text","default":"TOP 5 SHOPPING MISTAKES"},{"type":"html","id":"gLDSSkMrKvIUY_text","label":"gLDSSkMrKvIUY_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#EA0B0B;\"><strong>Sourcing Matters:</strong></span> Beware of Shilajit not sourced from high-altitude regions like the Himalayas. Shilajit from lower altitude regions lacks purity and potency</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gPZyrPPAQzsUF_text","label":"gPZyrPPAQzsUF_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#EA0B0B;\"><strong>Cheap Shilajit</strong></span>: Shilajit isn't cheap, even in India. AMzN is filled with garbage. These brands drop-ship \"shilajit\" straight from China to your door. Don't buy anything under $30- it's not real.*</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gTWopkFhNlVMB_text","label":"gTWopkFhNlVMB_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#EA0B0B;\"><strong>Lack of Lab Testing:</strong></span> Don't buy from brands that don't test for heavy metals, contaminants, and salmonella. Since it's an organic material, you want it to be tested..</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gMujuoVohcjQE_text","label":"gMujuoVohcjQE_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#EA0B0B;\"><strong>Low Fulvic Acid:</strong></span> Watch for products with low fulvic acid content (below 70%). Products with low fulvic acid ratios won't provide optimal benefits.</p>"}],
